                "added": [
                    "#* If you cannot extinguish the fire within five seconds of using the extinguisher, then it’s too large. Evacuate to a safe place and call 911.",
                    "#Call 911. Even if the fire is out, you should still call 911. Smoldering objects can reignite, and proper firefighters will be able to isolate and remove any risks completely.[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 7 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#* If you cannot extinguish the fire within five seconds of using the extinguisher, then it’s too large. Evacuate to a safe place and call 911.",
                    "#Call 911. Even if the fire is out, you should still call 911. Smoldering objects can reignite, and proper firefighters will be able to isolate and remove any risks completely.[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 11 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#* To use the extinguisher, aim at the base of the fire and sweep the spray back and forth across it until it’s out.",
                    "#* If you cannot extinguish the fire within five seconds of using the extinguisher, then it’s too large. Evacuate to a safe place and call 911.",
                    "*Any time you cannot extinguish the fire within five seconds of using the extinguisher, then it’s too large. The extinguisher will likely run out before you put out the fire. Evacuate to a safe place and call 911."
                ],
                "removed": [
