        {
            "id": "11199047",
            "user": "Wikiphoto",
            "timestamp": "22:06, 23 September 2013",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(6,371 bytes)",
            "change": 125,
            "summary": "(Enlarging and centering Steps photos)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "reverted",
            "contribution_type": "addition",
            "reverted_by": "Jack Pearce",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#'''If a fire has taken hold,''' (spread to other areas or structures or the smoke has is at head height), all occupants of that building must be [[Pull a Fire Alarm|alerted]] and evacuated. Note to all: Do not fight a fire not worth fighting, evacuate the building; personal safety comes first.<br><br>[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 1.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Contact the fire brigade as soon as possible.<br><br>[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "# Turn off all power to the fire, usually done by turning off the main power. This step alone is usually enough to stop most fires in the initial stages.<br><br>[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 3.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Use a safety blanket to smother the fire (Remember: If you do not turn off the power supply, electric shock is likely to occur.). Not only is this very effective in the early stages but does not damage surrounding area or objects.<br><br>[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 4.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Use water (more than two liters at a time) to extinguish the fire, throw the water at the base or seat of the fire. This is also very effective, but not recommended due to the damage it may cause. It is only effective in the early stages of a fire.(Remember: If you do not turn off the main power supply, electric shock is likely to occur).<br><br>[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 5.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#The safest and the best way to extinguish a electrical fire is to use a fire extinguisher. Follow the instructions on it for more information. '''Note''': During the initial stages of fire, once the fire is put out the surfaces that it has touched or burned are very hot and are likely to catch fire. You must have enough extinguishing material for at least 7 extinguishing attempts. E.G. 6Kg dry powder fire extinguisher. (Remember: If you do not turn of the mains power supply, electric shock is likely to occur).Aim the extinguisher nozzle at the base or seat of a fire for most effective extinguishing of fire.<br><br>[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 6.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Never throw water on a liquid fire. This is due to water and oils properties. If the water is thrown on the fire, the following will occur.<br><br>[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 7.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Water does not mix with the oil, and thus goes underneath it (oil and water don't mix; when they are together oil is on top water on bottom). It will then boil and become steam '''very quickly''' this quick boil is dangerous . Since the water is on the bottom of the oil, as it evaporates it sprays hot, burning oil in every direction. This then spreads the fire and usually leaves you unconscious.<br><br>[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 8.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Use a safety blanket and smother the fire, this is particularly useful at home. Use this only if the fire is small enough for you to cover.<br><br>[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 9.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Use a fire extinguisher. Remember to read the instructions very carefully. If the extinguisher instructs you to not use it on a liquid or chemical fire, do not use it. Call the fire brigade and evacuate the building.<br><br>[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 10.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Use lots of water to smother the fire. This is the best and quickest solution in the early stages.<br><br>[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 11.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Use a safety blanket to smother the fire in its early stages. Remember to cover the fire completely and wait ten minutes.<br><br>[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 12.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Use a fire extinguisher; most will work on organic fires. Never forget to read the instructions on the extinguisher. Follow them to the letter.<br><br>[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 13.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#  If you smell gas or see a dangerous situation involving flammable gas, or any gas for that matter contact the fire brigade immediately, and evacuate to a safe distance.<br><br>[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 14.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "",
                    ""
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "",
                    "#[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 1.jpg|right|300px]]'''If a fire has taken hold,''' (spread to other areas or structures or the smoke has is at head height), all occupants of that building must be [[Pull a Fire Alarm|alerted]] and evacuated. Note to all: Do not fight a fire not worth fighting, evacuate the building; personal safety comes first.",
                    "#[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 2.jpg|right|300px]]Contact the fire brigade as soon as possible.",
                    "# [[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 3.jpg|right|300px]]Turn off all power to the fire, usually done by turning off the main power. This step alone is usually enough to stop most fires in the initial stages.",
                    "#[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 4.jpg|right|300px]]Use a safety blanket to smother the fire (Remember: If you do not turn off the power supply, electric shock is likely to occur.). Not only is this very effective in the early stages but does not damage surrounding area or objects.",
                    "#[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 5.jpg|right|300px]]Use water (more than two liters at a time) to extinguish the fire, throw the water at the base or seat of the fire. This is also very effective, but not recommended due to the damage it may cause. It is only effective in the early stages of a fire.(Remember: If you do not turn off the main power supply, electric shock is likely to occur).",
                    "#[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 6.jpg|right|300px]]The safest and the best way to extinguish a electrical fire is to use a fire extinguisher. Follow the instructions on it for more information. '''Note''': During the initial stages of fire, once the fire is put out the surfaces that it has touched or burned are very hot and are likely to catch fire. You must have enough extinguishing material for at least 7 extinguishing attempts. E.G. 6Kg dry powder fire extinguisher. (Remember: If you do not turn of the mains power supply, electric shock is likely to occur).Aim the extinguisher nozzle at the base or seat of a fire for most effective extinguishing of fire.",
                    "#[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 7.jpg|right|300px]]Never throw water on a liquid fire. This is due to water and oils properties. If the water is thrown on the fire, the following will occur.",
                    "#[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 8.jpg|right|300px]]Water does not mix with the oil, and thus goes underneath it (oil and water don't mix; when they are together oil is on top water on bottom). It will then boil and become steam '''very quickly''' this quick boil is dangerous . Since the water is on the bottom of the oil, as it evaporates it sprays hot, burning oil in every direction. This then spreads the fire and usually leaves you unconscious.",
                    "#[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 9.jpg|right|300px]]Use a safety blanket and smother the fire, this is particularly useful at home. Use this only if the fire is small enough for you to cover.",
                    "#[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 10.jpg|right|300px]]Use a fire extinguisher. Remember to read the instructions very carefully. If the extinguisher instructs you to not use it on a liquid or chemical fire, do not use it. Call the fire brigade and evacuate the building.",
                    "#[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 11.jpg|right|300px]]Use lots of water to smother the fire. This is the best and quickest solution in the early stages.",
                    "#[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 12.jpg|right|300px]]Use a safety blanket to smother the fire in its early stages. Remember to cover the fire completely and wait ten minutes.",
                    "#[[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 13.jpg|right|300px]]Use a fire extinguisher; most will work on organic fires. Never forget to read the instructions on the extinguisher. Follow them to the letter.",
                    "#  [[Image:Extinguish a Fire at the Initial Stages Step 14.jpg|right|300px]]If you smell gas or see a dangerous situation involving flammable gas, or any gas for that matter contact the fire brigade immediately, and evacuate to a safe distance."
                ]
            }
        },
